cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "cqtna: Context-Specific QTL Target Nomination Audit"
abstract: >-
  An audit for candidate lists produced by cis-eQTL-instrumented Mendelian
  randomization. Runs the automatable part of eight diagnostics and reports what
  kind of evidence each nominated gene carries. Three of the eight cannot be
  automated from a candidate list and are named in every report rather than
  omitted; no gene reaches "target-supported" from this tool.
type: software
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/cqtna"
keywords:
  - Mendelian randomization
  - expression quantitative trait loci
  - target nomination
  - colocalisation
  - reproducibility
authors:
  - name: "MR audit project"
